---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SubstackEmbed from '../components/SubstackEmbed.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Jonathan A. Hutton"
  description="Jonathan A. Hutton is a builder who turns organizational ambiguity into finished, working structure — plus the book Unflappable, flying, and what's next."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>About</h1>

      <!-- DRAFT bio — reframed to the "systems-level change agent" through-line.
           Grounded in real facts; Jonathan to review/approve wording. -->
      <p>
        I'm a builder, and the through-line across everything I make is
        <strong>change</strong>. I take organizational ambiguity and turn it into
        elegant, working structure — software, systems, teams, physical spaces,
        organizations, and the written word. I'm at my best from a blank sheet,
        standing up something that didn't exist before, and I care most about the
        change the work causes — not the process around it.
      </p>

      <p>
        That's looked like a lot of things: founding a cross-functional business
        architecture team inside a state agency; leading a 20,000-SKU e-commerce
        migration through an ownership change; helping revive a dormant nonprofit;
        designing and shipping a live civic platform end to end; and remodeling a
        kitchen down to the studs. Enterprise architecture and civic technology on
        one side, hands-on building and design on the other — same instinct, turning
        a mess into a finished thing.
      </p>

      <!-- Credibility signal -->
      <h2>Recognition</h2>
      <!-- TODO(jon): confirm/adjust this one-sentence framing before launch. -->
      <p>
        My reconstructive surgeon at UW Medicine, Dr. Barber, is interviewing me
        for a department-wide grand rounds talk based in part on my story.
      </p>

      <!-- DRAFT paragliding section — plain register, ties to the hero photo and the
           book. Craft Jon cares about: he may want to take the pen here. -->
      <h2>Flying</h2>
      <p>
        When I'm not building something, I'm usually flying. Paragliding is a launch,
        a read of the air, and a commitment — no engine, no second chances at the
        decision. It's also where a lot of the book came from. Being sick grounded me
        for a while; getting back on a hillside with a wing laid out was part of
        finding my way through.
      </p>

      <h2>The book</h2>
      <p>
        I wrote <em>Unflappable: Soaring Beyond a Diagnosis</em>, a memoir about
        rare disease, paragliding, and finding healing even when cures are out of
        reach — published at
        <a href={site.bookUrl} rel="noopener">unflappable.press</a>. A second book,
        on patient and provider stories in head and neck reconstructive surgery, is
        in progress.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SubstackEmbed heading="Follow the work" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose p { font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: var(--space-12); }
</style>
